.TH P9SHARE-MOUNTS 5 "2026" "p9share" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
p9share-mounts \- the shares a machine shows, for p9share
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I /etc/p9share/mounts
has one mount per line, three fields separated by white space:
.RS
.nf
USER NAME MOUNTPOINT
.fi
.RE
.TP
.I USER
The account on this machine that the exporting machine logs in to.  Its socket
.IR ~USER/.p9share/NAME.sock
is what is mounted, and only if that socket is owned by USER.
.TP
.I NAME
The name the exporter gave the share.
.TP
.I MOUNTPOINT
An absolute path (letters, digits and  . _ + @ \- / only), created if missing.
.PP
Blank lines and text after # are ignored.  The file is written by
.B p9share mount
and
.BR "p9share unmount" ,
and may be edited by hand; the daemon re-reads it every two seconds.  A mountpoint that already holds something that is not 9p is left alone.
.PP
The user's mode for the mount (rw, ro or off) is in
.IR ~USER/.config/p9share/mode.d/NAME ,
written by
.BR "p9share rw|ro|off NAME" .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR p9share (8),
.BR p9share\-exports (5)
